{"abstract":"Purpose: To assess the use of quantitative diffusion-weighted MRI (DW-MRI) as a diagnostic imaging biomarker in differentiating between benign colon adenoma, early, and advanced cancer of the colon, as well as predicting lymph node involvement, and finally comparing mucinous-producing colon cancer with adenomas and non-mucinous colon cancer. Method: Patients with a confirmed tumor on colonoscopy were eligible for inclusion in this study. Using a 3.0 Tesla MRI machine, the main tumor mean apparent diffusion coefficient (mADC) was obtained. Surgically resected tumor specimens served as an endpoint, except in mucinous colon cancers, which were classified based on T2 images. Results: A total of 152 patients were included in the study population. The mean age was 71 years. A statistically significant mADC mean difference of −282 × 10 −6 mm 2/s [−419–−144 95% CI, p < 0.001] was found between colon adenomas and early colon cancer, with an AUC of 0.80 [0.68–0.93 95% CI] and an optimal cut off value of 1018 × 10 −6 mm 2/s. Only a small statistically significant difference (p = 0.039) in mADC was found between benign tumors and mucinous colon cancer. We found no statistical difference in mADC mean values between early and advanced colon cancer, and between colon cancer with and without lymph node involvement. Conclusion: Quantitative DW-MRI is potentially useful for determining whether a colonic tumor is benign or malignant. Mucinous colon cancer shows less diffusion restriction when compared to non-mucinous colon cancer, a potential pitfall.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Otto, Peter Obel","Loft, Martina Kastrup","Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-714318"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils"],"keyword":["ADC","Adenoma","Colon cancer","DWI","Diffusion weighted imaging","MRI","Mucinous"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diffusion weighted mri as a quantitative imaging biomarker in colon tumors","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers16010144","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-714318","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10778248","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85182231555","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38201571","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-8a3e51be-8a9c-41b1-9284-fc7e76bead16"],"keyword":["ADC","DWI","MRI","adenoma","colon cancer","diffusion weighted imaging","mucinous"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-64D2482C4C65C2612094FC5BD2991FBD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers16010144","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/252167536/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Radiology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Obel","key":"ottopau","last":"Otto","locid":"af8af8d3-9114-4634-b2a4-3069f4b82701","name":"Otto, Peter Obel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martina Kastrup","key":"loftpau","last":"Loft","locid":"2f5b01a6-c7e9-4a6e-a810-9b95b154d58d","name":"Loft, Martina Kastrup","orcid":"0000-0003-3463-8574","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Rafael","key":"rafaelsenpau","last":"Rafaelsen","locid":"89253a87-a28b-4cb9-aa20-ded9a9d49536","name":"Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","orcid":"0000-0001-5182-5545","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Roland Vils","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c30865f6-a1d6-4198-a239-5679a60ef5f6","name":"Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils","orcid":"0000-0001-5167-7968","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38201571"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cancers16010144","issn":["20726694"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cancers","paperid":"144","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Cancers","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182231555"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8a3e51be-8a9c-41b1-9284-fc7e76bead16"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Diffusion-Weighted MRI as a Quantitative Imaging Biomarker in Colon Tumors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-714318","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Green macroalgae of the Ulva genus have gained interest as a source of protein, due to the high production potential and high proportion of essential amino acids. This review gives an overview of Ulva protein, including extraction and evaluation of protein quality in terms of nutritional value, functionality, and sensory properties with preliminary suggestions to reach the market. Scope and approach: Available literature on protein extraction from Ulva was reviewed along with studies investigating the nutritional quality of Ulva protein and functional properties including aroma and flavor characteristics. Opportunities, challenges, and knowledge gaps are presented. Key findings and conclusion: A range of studies are investigating protein extraction, but only a few studies have dealt with protein digestibility, and food protein products. The digestibility of protein in crude Ulva biomass is low compared to conventional protein sources but increase with protein extraction. Sensory and functionality studies on Ulva protein are yet absent, but the whole biomass has been investigated, indicating the potential. The lack of consisting studies calls for more investigations related to food quality of Ulva protein. Upscaling and biorefinery models need to be explored to unfold the true potential of Ulva as a source of food protein.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pedersen, Louise Juul","Nissen, Signe Hjerrild","Bruhn, Annette","Alexi, Niki","Jensen, Søren Krogh","Hammershøj, Marianne","Dalsgaard, Trine Kastrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-744844"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Dalsgaard, Trine Kastrup"],"keyword":["Food quality","Nutritional value","Protein digestibility","Protein extraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i ulva i species a critical review on the green seaweed as a source of food protein","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85193808014","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-744844","identifier":[{"id":"85193808014","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-91c7b008-2020-4f4b-878b-857ca16ac4b3"],"keyword":["Food quality","Functional and sensory properties","Nutritional value","Protein digestibility","Protein extraction","Ulva protein"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E625938711BD77209EE6CB560405A5EF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum - CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Agro Food Park","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"264ede20-2da8-4436-b58c-0488cf8a9760","name":"Pedersen, Louise Juul","name_org":"Juul, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-2719-1447","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe Hjerrild","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","locid":"8b86740f-37fd-4640-bcf8-0a6967919be8","name":"Nissen, Signe Hjerrild","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"bruhnpau","last":"Bruhn","locid":"15559017-3036-4e04-968e-338a24d800ce","name":"Bruhn, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-7940-1338","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niki","key":"alexipau","last":"Alexi","locid":"4cb15bc8-b447-4fcd-bbb1-0f1a727e2284","name":"Alexi, Niki","orcid":"0000-0001-9781-3611","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Krogh","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"7e493d39-1152-46c0-a822-c46e6ed914f3","name":"Jensen, Søren Krogh","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne","key":"hammershøjpau","last":"Hammershøj","locid":"483a27e1-b030-4e4b-8441-76424c064fed","name":"Hammershøj, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0001-9297-6526","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine Kastrup","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"5627b57a-8751-4959-bbaf-dd5871851aa3","name":"Dalsgaard, Trine Kastrup","orcid":"0000-0002-5635-4102","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tifs.2024.104534","issn":["09242244","09680020"],"issn_org":["09242244"],"journal":"Trends in Food Science and Technology","paperid":"104534","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Trends in Food Science and Technology","title_org":"Trends in Food Science & Technology","volume":"149"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85193808014"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-91c7b008-2020-4f4b-878b-857ca16ac4b3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"<i>Ulva </i>species: A critical review on the green seaweed as a source of food protein","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-744844","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Osteoarthritis (OA) affects 20% of the adult Danish population, and the financial burden to society amounts to DKK 4.6 billion annually. Research suggests that up to 75% of surgical patients could have postponed an operation and managed with physical training. ERVIN.2 is an artificial intelligence (AI)-based clinical support system that addresses this problem by enhancing patient involvement in decisions concerning surgical knee and hip replacement. However, the clinical outcomes and cost-effectiveness of using such a system are scantily documented. Objective: The primary objective is to investigate whether the usual care is non-inferior to ERVIN.2 supported care. The second objective is to determine if ERVIN.2 enhances clinical decision support and whether ERVIN.2 supported care is cost-effective. Methods: This study used a single-centre, non-inferiority, randomised controlled in a two-arm parallel-group design. The study will be reported in compliance with CONSORT guidelines. The control group receives the usual care. As an add-on, the intervention group have access to baseline scores and predicted Oxford hip/knee scores and HRQoL for both the surgical and the non-surgical trajectory. A cost-utility analysis will be conducted alongside the trial using a hospital perspective, a 1-year time horizon and effects estimated using EQ-5D-3L. Results will be presented as cost per QALY gain. Discussion: This study will bring knowledge about whether ERVIN.2 enhances clinical decision support, clinical effects, and cost-effectiveness of the AI system. The study design will not allow for the blinding of surgeons. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov NCT04332055. Registered on 2 April 2020.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hermansen, Nanna Kastrup","Bjerregaard, Helene H.","Laursen, Mogens Berg","Valentin, Jan Brink","Johnsen, Søren Paaske","Jensen, Cathrine Elgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107698"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hermansen, Nanna Kastrup"],"keyword":["Adult","Artificial intelligence","Clinical decision support system","Cost Benefit Analysis","Cost effectiveness","Decision Support Systems Clinical","Humans","Knee Joint surgery","Machine learning","Osteoarthritis","Patient reported outcomes","Randomised controlled trial","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Total hip replacement","Total knee replacement"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Regionernes Kliniske Kvalitetsudviklingsprogram (RKKP)"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an ai based patient specific clinical decision support system for oa patients choosing surgery or not study protocol for a single centre parallel group non inferiority randomised controlled trial","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-022-07039-5","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank Andreas Kappel for supporting the implementation of the system, giving feedback on flowcharts and re-educating the intervention doctors when using ERVIN.2. Thanks to Heidi L. Poulsen and Gitte B. Hansen for assisting with data collection, recruitment, practical and administrative issues. Thanks to Johanne H. Winther for setting up the REDCap module for randomisation."],"id":"S01-000.00-107698","identifier":[{"id":"85146271340","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36635747","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-c69c752d-0ca1-416d-959d-081478303692"],"keyword":["Adult","Artificial intelligence","Clinical decision support system","Cost-Benefit Analysis","Cost-effectiveness","Decision Support Systems, Clinical","Humans","Knee Joint/surgery","Machine learning","Osteoarthritis","Patient-reported outcomes","Randomised controlled trial","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Total hip replacement","Total knee replacement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D75103A5C06D44DAAD8A692F7E88E74B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/515394521/Kastrup_et_al._2023_._An_AI_based_patient_specific_clinical_decision_support_system_for_OA_patients_choosing_surgery_or_not_study_protocol_for_a_single_centre_parallel_group_non_inferiority_randomised_controlled_trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-022-07039-5","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Danish Center for Healthcare Improvements"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Regionernes Kliniske Kvalitetsudviklingsprogram (RKKP)"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nanna","key":"kastruppau","last":"Kastrup","locid":"65df2592-42f2-4677-bfc7-7f2d1f37dd91","name":"Hermansen, Nanna Kastrup","name_org":"Kastrup, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0003-0554-9994","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Helene H.","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","name":"Bjerregaard, Helene H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"26102317-00ee-41ec-ae85-c7a3bde4c391","name":"Laursen, Mogens Berg","name_org":"Laursen, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-2791-3921","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan B.","key":"valentinpau","last":"Valentin","locid":"4fbcfaf7-a4af-46c9-b3b4-f113b45baf05","name":"Valentin, Jan Brink","name_org":"Valentin, Jan B.","orcid":"0000-0002-8205-7179","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren P.","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"c3e8b374-a343-484a-a10d-e6550efbb8dc","name":"Johnsen, Søren Paaske","name_org":"Johnsen, Søren P.","orcid":"0000-0002-2787-0271","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cathrine E.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"078e71ca-9113-46d8-907c-9ec548aa6792","name":"Jensen, Cathrine Elgaard","name_org":"Jensen, Cathrine E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36635747"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13063-022-07039-5","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issn_org":["17456215"],"journal":"Trials","paperid":"24","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Trials","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146271340"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c69c752d-0ca1-416d-959d-081478303692"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An AI-based patient-specific clinical decision support system for OA patients choosing surgery or not : study protocol for a single-centre, parallel-group, non-inferiority randomised controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107698","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Endorectal ultrasound (ERUS) is an important tool when evaluating complex rectal adenomas and rectal cancer, and the accuracy is improved by adding elastography measurements. A high interobserver agreement is imperative in clinical practice. Therefore, the aim of this study was to evaluate interobserver agreement assessed on real-time images. Additionally, we investigated the intra-and interobserver agreement between experienced and inexperienced observers. Materials and methods: We prospectively included patients referred to an ERUS at the Department of Radiology with a complex rectal polyp or suspected rectal malignancy. Two operators independently scanned each patient in turn. Furthermore, four observers assessed previously obtained images using three different methods for placing the region of interest (ROI). Three months later, the four observers reassessed the images to assess intraobserver variability. Results: A total of 19 patients were included for live assessment. Agreement of tumor classification was substantial for T stage (kappa: 0.86) and fair for N stage (kappa: 0.73), with an absolute agreement for T and N stages of 84% and 89%, respectively. Agreement of SWE was good for Emean (ICC 0.94, 95% CI 0.86–0.98) and fair for Emax (ICC 0.85, 95% CI 0.66–0.94). Intra-and interobserver agreement between inexperienced and experienced observers showed good to excellent agreement with all ROI methods. Conclusion: Interobserver agreement is high in SWE when performed in a clinical setting. We found the best agreement using the mean value of several ROIs. Intra-and interobserver agreement was high regardless of operator experience.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Loft, Martina Kastrup","Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils","Grimm, Peter","Lauritzen, Andreas Hoffmann","Dam, Claus","Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-625800"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Loft, Martina Kastrup"],"keyword":["Interobserver","Rectal Neoplasms","Reproducibility","Shear wave elastography","Ultrasound"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intra and interobserver variability of shear wave elastography in rectal cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers14112633","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: This research was funded by Aage and Johanne Louis-Hansens Fond, grant number 20-2B-6754. This research was funded by Aage and Johanne Louis-Hansens Fond, grant number 20-2B-6754.Study data were collected and managed using REDCap electronic data capture tools hosted by OPEN, Open Patient data Explorative Network, Odense University Hospital, Region of Southern Denmark [23,24]."],"id":"S01-000.00-625800","identifier":[{"id":"35681613","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85131631689","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9179262","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-b769cb48-14d3-41fe-81d5-a2d455ebb439"],"keyword":["interobserver","rectal neoplasms","reproducibility","shear wave elastography","ultrasound"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52596CB06FE2E23AD4094A4D0A6F9E86"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers14112633","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/204197139/cancers_14_02633.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Radiology (Vejle)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Urology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Sygehus Lillebælt"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martina Kastrup","key":"loftpau","last":"Loft","locid":"2f5b01a6-c7e9-4a6e-a810-9b95b154d58d","name":"Loft, Martina Kastrup","orcid":"0000-0003-3463-8574","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Roland Vils","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c30865f6-a1d6-4198-a239-5679a60ef5f6","name":"Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils","orcid":"0000-0001-5167-7968","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"grimmpau","last":"Grimm","locid":"d40a89a6-1347-45d7-a7c7-1a83da13dfac","name":"Grimm, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-0927-4609","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Hoffmann","key":"lauritzenpau","last":"Lauritzen","name":"Lauritzen, Andreas Hoffmann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","locid":"103f5188-29ea-414d-ac02-ab5253a7e41b","name":"Dam, Claus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Rafael","key":"rafaelsenpau","last":"Rafaelsen","locid":"89253a87-a28b-4cb9-aa20-ded9a9d49536","name":"Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","orcid":"0000-0001-5182-5545","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35681613"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cancers14112633","issn":["20726694"],"issue":"11","journal":"Cancers","paperid":"2633","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Cancers","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131631689"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b769cb48-14d3-41fe-81d5-a2d455ebb439"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Intra-and Interobserver Variability of Shear Wave Elastography in Rectal Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-625800","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To investigate the diagnostic performance of endorectal ultrasound (ERUS), shear-wave elastography (SWE), and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) in patients with a complex rectal adenoma or an early rectal cancer, i.e., T1 or T2 adenocarcinoma in a clinical setting, and to evaluate the association between SWE and stromal fraction (SF) and apparent diffusion coefficient (ADC) and SF. METHOD: This prospective study included patients undergoing ERUS and SWE for a rectal tumor subsequently confirmed by histopathology to be an adenoma or a T1 or T2 adenocarcinoma. The accuracy of the imaging methods was assessed by comparing the T category as determined by ERUS and MRI with histopathology, which served as the gold standard. SF was assessed on surgical specimens. RESULTS: A total of 86 patients were included. Of these, 62 patients had adenomas and 24 patients had carcinomas, of which 11 were T1 tumors and 13 were T2 tumors. ERUS and MRI yielded sensitivity, specificity, and accuracy of 0.79 and 0.73, 0.95 and 0.90, and 0.86 and 0.78, respectively, for discrimination between benign and malignant lesions. The area under the receiver operating characteristics curve for SWE was 0.88, and with a cut-off value of 40 kPa the sensitivity, specificity, and accuracy were 0.79, 0.89, and 0.86, respectively. There was a positive correlation between SF and SWE with a p-value of &lt;0.001 and a negative correlation between SF and ADC with a p-value of 0.011. CONCLUSION: Both ERUS and MRI classified T categories with a high accuracy; however, ERUS classified more adenomas correctly than MRI. In this small population, SWE could differentiate an adenoma from early carcinoma. SF was correlated with both SWE and ADC, as increasing SF tended to yield higher SWE and lower ADC values.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Loft, Martina Kastrup","Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils","Lindebjerg, Jan","Rahr, Hans B","Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-605186"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Loft, Martina Kastrup"],"keyword":["Diffusion weighted imaging","Endorectal ultrasound","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Rectal cancer","Shear wave elastography","Tumor stroma ratio"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"endorectal ultrasound shear wave elastography of complex rectal adenoma and early rectal cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics12092166","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was supported by Lillebaelt Hospital Research Grants and Aage and Johanne Louis-Hansen’s Fond, grant number 20-2B-6754."],"id":"S01-000.00-605186","identifier":[{"id":"85138611942","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36140566","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9497521","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-6fc2cd71-06c6-4efa-934b-41649d0c093b"],"keyword":["diffusion-weighted imaging","endorectal ultrasound","magnetic resonance imaging","rectal adenoma","rectal cancer","shear-wave elastography","stromal fraction","tumor–stroma ratio"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5BBA395917E48CE3C9E0453C4D5BDCC5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics12092166","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/207122826/diagnostics_12_02166.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Radiology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martina Kastrup","key":"loftpau","last":"Loft","locid":"2f5b01a6-c7e9-4a6e-a810-9b95b154d58d","name":"Loft, Martina Kastrup","orcid":"0000-0003-3463-8574","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Roland","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c30865f6-a1d6-4198-a239-5679a60ef5f6","name":"Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils","name_org":"Pedersen, Malene Roland","orcid":"0000-0001-5167-7968","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"lindebjergpau","last":"Lindebjerg","locid":"5de10dbb-de45-4c38-8ed2-35bd614d5459","name":"Lindebjerg, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-2055-4241","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans B","key":"rahrpau","last":"Rahr","locid":"941e7830-92a2-42c8-a6d4-93a9fa3235e4","name":"Rahr, Hans B","orcid":"0000-0002-4571-7852","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"rafaelsenpau","last":"Rafaelsen","locid":"89253a87-a28b-4cb9-aa20-ded9a9d49536","name":"Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","name_org":"Rafaelsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0001-5182-5545","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36140566"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/diagnostics12092166","issn":["20754418"],"issue":"9","journal":"Diagnostics","paperid":"2166","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Diagnostics","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138611942"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6fc2cd71-06c6-4efa-934b-41649d0c093b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Endorectal Ultrasound Shear-Wave Elastography of Complex Rectal Adenoma and Early Rectal Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-605186","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Many seaweed species have a high production potential and attract interest as future protein sources. A high fiber and ash content, however, demand extraction of the protein to improve its digestibility and protein utilization in food or feed. This study explores three different approaches for protein extraction from Ulva fenestrata in order to maximize the protein extraction yield. Soluble protein was recovered either by mechanical pressing or by homogenization and osmotic shock of the biomass followed by alkaline extraction. The soluble protein was then concentrated by isoelectric precipitation. A combined procedure was carried out by pressing the biomass and following subjecting the residual pulp fraction to homogenization, osmotic shock and alkaline extraction. The three methods were ranked as follows with respect to protein extraction yield (as % of biomass protein); the combined method (23.9 ± 0.3%)> the alkaline extraction (6.8 ± 0.2%)> mechanical pressing (5.0 ± 0.2%). The significant increase when combining the methods was ascribed to a high precipitation yield after alkaline extraction of the pulp, hypothesized to be due to a reduced conductivity of the alkali-soluble protein fraction when derived from pulp rather than whole biomass.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pedersen, Louise Juul","Steinhagen, S.","Bruhn, Annette","Jensen, Søren Krogh","Undeland, I.","Dalsgaard, Trine Kastrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-186079"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Dalsgaard, Trine Kastrup"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Alkaline extraction","Mechanical pressing","Precipitation","Protein extraction","Seaweed","Ulva"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combining pressing and alkaline extraction to increase protein yield from ulva fenestrata biomass","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fbp.2022.05.006","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-186079","identifier":[{"id":"85130728850","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-635e6f54-b73b-4607-b623-c1ff5ba4f921"],"keyword":["Alkaline extraction","Mechanical pressing","Precipitation","Protein extraction","Seaweed","Ulva"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2AD3E865BE47E3CEE125504B80F46A16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/300511986/1_s2.0_S0960308522000529_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fbp.2022.05.006","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"264ede20-2da8-4436-b58c-0488cf8a9760","name":"Pedersen, Louise Juul","name_org":"Juul, L.","orcid":"0000-0002-2719-1447","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"steinhagenpau","last":"Steinhagen","name":"Steinhagen, S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.","key":"bruhnpau","last":"Bruhn","locid":"15559017-3036-4e04-968e-338a24d800ce","name":"Bruhn, Annette","name_org":"Bruhn, A.","orcid":"0000-0002-7940-1338","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. K.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"7e493d39-1152-46c0-a822-c46e6ed914f3","name":"Jensen, Søren Krogh","name_org":"Jensen, S. K.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"I.","key":"undelandpau","last":"Undeland","name":"Undeland, I.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"T. K.","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"5627b57a-8751-4959-bbaf-dd5871851aa3","name":"Dalsgaard, Trine Kastrup","name_org":"Dalsgaard, T. K.","orcid":"0000-0002-5635-4102","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fbp.2022.05.006","issn":["09603085","17443571"],"issn_org":["09603085"],"journal":"Food and Bioproducts Processing","pages":"80-85","publisher":"Institution of Chemical Engineers","status":"p","title":"Food and Bioproducts Processing","volume":"134"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130728850"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-635e6f54-b73b-4607-b623-c1ff5ba4f921"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Combining pressing and alkaline extraction to increase protein yield from Ulva fenestrata biomass","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&