{"abstract":"For potato proteins to be used as a food ingredient, the level of natural potato defense substances, the glycoalkaloids (GAs), should be limited. In this work, a method is developed for quantification of the two major potato GAs, α-solanine and α-chaconine, as well as for their aglycon form, solanidine, using liquid chromatography–mass spectrometry single quadrupole in single ion monitoring mode. Standard solutions of GA and a food-grade potato protein powder was used to validate the method. A linear correlation between GA concentration and the ion intensity of >0.995 was obtained for all standard solutions. Recovery of GA in spiked samples was within the range 82%–106%. The method for GA quantification was applied to a variety of potato protein isolates. The results showed that total GA increased during the storage of the potatoes. Washing the potato protein isolates using water at a sufficient level was shown to be able to reduce the amount of GA below the threshold of 150 µg g−1, as needed for human consumption.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","Schmidt, Jesper Malling","Kristiansen, Gitte Hald","Dalsgaard, Trine Kastrup","Larsen, Lotte Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-183017"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Glycoalkaloid","Plant protein","Potato protein","Sustainability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liquid chromatography mass spectrometry quantification of α solanine α chaconine and solanidine in potato protein isolates","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/foods9040416","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-183017","identifier":[{"id":"32252270","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7230682","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85082737927","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5e232f40-242e-4ee0-964a-ae096e7a3dae"],"keyword":["Glycoalkaloid","Plant protein","Potato protein","Single ion monitoring","Sustainability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-73C45ADDAAEB014DE5C3BD2C2E49616C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/foods9040416","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Food Science, Department of Food Science - Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Drud-Heydary","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"030ede5c-2e12-40c1-9d0c-543f0c5ffadf","name":"Nielsen, Søren Drud-Heydary","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Malling","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"a01f95f3-f57f-457f-bbab-7812db1648ae","name":"Schmidt, Jesper Malling","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte Hald","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"82722678-5af2-4c59-9536-648f555c249a","name":"Kristiansen, Gitte Hald","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine Kastrup","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"5627b57a-8751-4959-bbaf-dd5871851aa3","name":"Dalsgaard, Trine Kastrup","orcid":"0000-0002-5635-4102","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte Bach","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"204d7240-6828-4ee0-8ef5-77a4a2ac92d4","name":"Larsen, Lotte Bach","orcid":"0000-0001-9674-0107","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32252270"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/foods9040416","issn":["23048158"],"issue":"4","journal":"Foods","paperid":"416","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Foods","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082737927"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5e232f40-242e-4ee0-964a-ae096e7a3dae"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Liquid Chromatography Mass Spectrometry Quantification of α-solanine, α-chaconine, and Solanidine in Potato Protein Isolates","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-183017","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The purpose of this study was to evaluate the effect of completeness of the radiological reports in primary local staging colon cancer when using a template. Methods: The study used primary staging reports retrieved from the departments RIS/PACS. Five key tumour descriptors were evaluated within each report: tumour morphology (polypoid or annular), information on tumour breach of the colon wall (≥ T3), tumour out-growth in mm, nodal status and TNM in conclusion. The failure to provide a description of the presence or absence of a feature in a report counted as ‘not reported’. To allow comparisons between reporting styles, the template or free-text style of reporting was also recorded. Results: During a two year period, a total of 666 patients CT reports were evaluated at the colorectal center multidisciplinary team (MDT) conference. In 200 of these reports a template was used. Information on tumour morphology (polypoid or annular) was present in 81% of the template reports vs 9% in free-text style. The figures in percentage for information on tumour breach of the colon wall (≥ T3) were 93% vs 48 %, tumour out-growth in mm: 51% vs 17%, nodal status: 99% vs 86% and TNM in conclusion: 98% vs 51%. P < 0.0001. Conclusion: The present study provides additional support for the routine use of template reports to improve imaging reporting standards in colonic cancer.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils","Dam, Claus","Loft, Martina Kastrup","Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-619364"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils"],"keyword":["Colon cancer","Computed tomography","Staging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reporting colon cancer staging using a template","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejro.2020.01.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-619364","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6994830","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32021880","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85078406666","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-a1476020-86f6-4b9d-afa9-1ab26665077d"],"keyword":["Colon cancer","Computed tomography","Staging","Template-reporting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-660201321401C965C7B7E182E5444110"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejro.2020.01.002","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/160343434/1_s2.0_S2352047720300022_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Radiology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Roland V.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c30865f6-a1d6-4198-a239-5679a60ef5f6","name":"Pedersen, Malene Roland Vils","name_org":"Pedersen, Malene Roland V.","orcid":"0000-0001-5167-7968","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","locid":"103f5188-29ea-414d-ac02-ab5253a7e41b","name":"Dam, Claus","rank":2,"rolecode":"p